Microsoft Learn: Configure Azure Blob Storage

Platform: Microsoft Learn
Module: Configure Azure Blob Storage
Track: AZ-104 Microsoft Azure Administrator
Difficulty: Intermediate
Date: 2026

Objective

Learn how to configure and manage Azure Blob Storage for scalable, high-performance storage of unstructured data in cloud environments.

This module focused on configuring Azure Blob Storage accounts, managing containers and blobs, optimizing storage costs through access tiers, and implementing lifecycle management and replication strategies for business continuity.

Step 1: Understanding Azure Blob Storage

The module introduced Azure Blob Storage as Microsoft’s object storage solution for unstructured data.

Types of unstructured data:
Video files
Images
Backups
Documents
Logs
Binary application data

The learning scenario focused on a media company storing thousands of video clips accessed daily by customers and internal systems.

Key Blob Storage benefits:
Massive scalability
High durability
Global availability
Cost optimization through storage tiers
Integration with AI and analytics workloads

Azure Blob Storage is designed for cloud-native applications that require large-scale object storage.

Step 2: Creating and Configuring Blob Storage

The module covered creating Azure Storage Accounts configured for Blob Storage workloads.

Key configuration areas:
Configuration	Purpose
