Secure data management is critical for enterprise cloud environments.

Step 4: Access Tiers and Cost Optimization

A major focus of the module was reducing storage costs through access tiers.

Azure Blob access tiers:
Tier	Best For
Hot	Frequently accessed data
Cool	Infrequently accessed data
Archive	Rarely accessed long-term storage
Important lessons learned:
Hot tier offers highest performance and lowest access latency
Cool tier lowers storage cost but increases access cost
Archive tier provides lowest storage cost with slower retrieval times

The media company scenario used lifecycle management to automatically move older videos into lower-cost tiers.

This demonstrated how Azure Administrators balance performance and operational costs.

Step 5: Lifecycle Management Policies

The module introduced lifecycle management automation for blob storage.

Lifecycle management capabilities:
Automatically move blobs between tiers
Delete expired data
Reduce long-term storage costs
Apply rule-based retention policies
Example automation strategies:
Move videos to Cool tier after 30 days
Archive older content after 180 days
Delete outdated files after retention periods expire

Lifecycle policies help organizations manage large-scale storage efficiently.

